{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries over sequences of any "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Sets of sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"],"anchor":"Sets-of-sequences"},{"title":"Dictionaries keyed by sequences","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"],"anchor":"Dictionaries-keyed-by-sequences"},{"title":"Pattern matching","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton"],"anchor":"Pattern-matching"},{"title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tries"]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","externalID":"Tries","title":"Tries","modules":[{"name":"Tries"}],"symbolKind":"module"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a set of sequences and a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a dictionary keyed by them, both kept in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a trie (Fredkin, 1960): a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex paths spell the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keys. They answer the queries a hash set cannot: every key with a prefix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"elements(withPrefix:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1)), whether any key has one ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPrefix(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the longest key that is a prefix of a query ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"longestPrefix(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"code":["import Tries","","let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keys are any sequence of the symbol type and are stored as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Symbol]"},{"type":"text","text":". For text, the symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type decides what a step is: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" steps by grapheme cluster, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by scalar, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"utf8"},{"type":"text","text":" by byte, the fastest of the three, because comparing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes is cheaper than comparing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Character"},{"type":"text","text":"s. When the symbols are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", each vertex keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its children sorted, so iteration is in lexicographic order; otherwise children come in the order"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"they were added."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree"},{"text":" and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary"},{"text":" hold the same keys and answer the same queries,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the same names, in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): every chain of vertices with one child and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols, so there is a vertex per key and per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"branching point rather than per symbol. They suit keys with long shared prefixes, such as file","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths or URLs, and build faster and in less memory than a trie of the same keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A trie’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"code":"PrefixTree","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"PrefixTree(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a radix tree’s to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"code":"Arborescence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its vertices’ prefixes with "},{"code":"Arborescence(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (import Grafluent’s "},{"code":"Trees","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module beside this one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" (Aho and Corasick, 1975) finds every occurrence of any of a set of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns in one pass over a text, in O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" + ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"z","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" symbols and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"z"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" matches: a trie of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patterns with failure links. Its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the automaton as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let automaton = AhoCorasickAutomaton(patterns: [\"he\", \"she\", \"his\", \"hers\"])","automaton.matches(in: \"ushers\").map(\\.patternIndex)   \/\/ [1, 0, 3]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trees":{"type":"topic","title":"Trees","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trees","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trees","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTree":{"type":"topic","title":"RadixTree","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTree","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every chain of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its symbols.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTree","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/TrieDictionary":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root-to-vertex paths spell the keys, each key’s vertex holding its value (Fredkin, 1960)."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"TrieDictionary","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/triedictionary","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TrieDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/TrieDictionary","type":"topic"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries":{"type":"topic","title":"Tries","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Tries over sequences of any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" symbols, with prefix queries, and multi-pattern matching.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/StatesView-swift.struct/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofEdgeAt","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.struct\/symbol(ofedgeat:)","title":"symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The symbol a goto edge reads, or nil for a failure edge.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/Trie":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/trie","kind":"symbol","title":"Trie","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/Trie","abstract":[{"text":"A set of sequences kept in a trie: a tree whose edges carry symbols and whose root-to-vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"paths spell the keys (Fredkin, 1960).","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Trie","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","abstract":[{"text":"An automaton that finds every occurrence of every pattern of a set in one pass over a text","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Aho and Corasick, 1975).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/AhoCorasickAutomaton/statesView-swift.property":{"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/ahocorasickautomaton\/statesview-swift.property","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/statesView-swift.property","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"title":"statesView","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The automaton’s states as a directed graph: a vertex per state, numbered from 0 for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"root, a goto edge from each state to each of its trie children, and a failure edge from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each state but the root to its failure state. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/AhoCorasickAutomaton\/StatesView-swift.struct\/symbol(ofEdgeAt:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" tells the two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"apart."}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"statesView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AhoCorasickAutomaton","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Symbol","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"StatesView","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Tries20AhoCorasickAutomatonV10StatesViewV","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Tries/documentation/Tries/RadixTreeDictionary":{"type":"topic","title":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tries\/documentation\/Tries\/RadixTreeDictionary","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dictionary keyed by sequences, kept in a radix tree (Morrison, 1968): a trie in which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chain of vertices with one child and no key is merged into one edge labelled with all its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols, each key’s vertex holding its value."}],"url":"\/documentation\/tries\/radixtreedictionary","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RadixTreeDictionary","kind":"identifier"}]}}}